target: skills/review/review-loop/review-stats.py
verify: cd skills/review/review-loop && ./review-stats.test.sh
expect: an unrecognised status 'error' goes loud and is named
why:    defaulting an unrecognised status to the DELIBERATE bucket softens every failure spelling nobody listed — error, timeout, crashed, blocked, incomplete, and FAILED all read as "declined with a reason". Neither vocabulary is closed, so the default is the whole decision, and it must be loud
--- old
            if st in DECLINED_STATES:
                declined[g] += 1
                decline_why[g].add(st)
            else:
                dropped[g] += 1
                drop_why[g].add(st)
--- new
            if st in ("unreported", "failed"):
                dropped[g] += 1
                drop_why[g].add(st)
            else:
                declined[g] += 1
                decline_why[g].add(st)
